development, even before revenue.

The list covers each named operator's hosting and compute platforms. Amazon
Bedrock alone is listed, not AWS generally. AWS infrastructure (such as
EC2), Microsoft Azure, Baseten, Google Cloud / AI Studio, Oracle Cloud,
private hardware, and unlisted platforms are allowed. Listing follows a
renamed operator or continuing service, not an acquirer's unrelated
businesses. The list is fixed: no revenue test or automatic additions
apply.

The named permitted providers may operate their own deployments on hardware
leased from listed operators if they actually manage serving. This does not
permit deployment inside a listed service, including Bedrock. Routing,
reselling, or relabeling cannot bypass the ban. Buying hardware,
downloading models, storage, DNS, transit, and unrelated API calls alone
are not deployment.

3. NO REWRITES FOR PROHIBITED DEPLOYMENTS

